## Change Management Configuration

### Change Authority Matrix
  STANDARD changes:
    Approval authority: [Role title] — process owner
    No CAB required
    Notice required: [N] business days

  SIGNIFICANT changes:
    Approval authority: [Role title] + [Function head]
    No CAB required but recommended for high-impact
    Notice required: [N] business days

  MAJOR changes:
    Approval authority: Change Advisory Board (CAB)
    CAB composition: [List roles — e.g. COO, IT Director, relevant function heads]
    Impact assessment: MANDATORY before CAB submission
    Notice required: [N] weeks minimum

  CRITICAL changes:
    Approval authority: [Executive sponsor] + CAB + [Legal/Compliance]
    Impact assessment: MANDATORY
    Board notification: Required
    Notice required: Formal programme governance

  EMERGENCY changes:
    On-call approval authority: [Role — available 24/7]
    Retrospective review: Within [N] business days
    Board notification: If P1 incident-driven

### CAB Schedule
  Frequency:  [Weekly / Bi-weekly / Monthly]
  Day / Time: [e.g. Every Tuesday 10:00]
  Chair:      [Change Manager name]
  Submission deadline: [N] business days before CAB

### Change Freeze Periods
  [Define periods when no MAJOR or CRITICAL changes are permitted]
  Year-end close:         [Dates — typically [month] last 2 weeks]
  Peak operational period:[Dates if applicable]
  Tax filing deadline:    [Dates if applicable]
  [Add any sector-specific freeze periods]

### Post-Implementation Review Requirements
  CRITICAL changes:  PIR mandatory; within 4 weeks of go-live
  MAJOR changes:     PIR mandatory; within 4 weeks of go-live
  SIGNIFICANT:       PIR recommended; within 6 weeks
  STANDARD:          PIR optional; log closure only

